      "note": "Inspected owner-supplied don-manuel-i-abella-central-school.png on 2026-10-08; capture date unknown. URL locates the site. Near-continuous northwest/interior, west and south/east canopy with individually distinguishable crowns; fan-shaped courtyard paths around visible low garden wedges and south entry planting. Preserve courtyard exposed wedges instead of blanket paving. Crowns may overhang classroom roofs; trunk fits stay within each observed crown. No shadow hedges or invented courtyard fixtures. Crown-width observations: Main northwest and southwest/southeast crowns about 70-90 px, smaller classroom gaps 35-60 px and tiny courtyard plants 25-35 px. Central red roof, western classroom row and fan-shaped south courtyard. Dense crowns obscure much of the yard. The upper west classroom corner is obscured by canopy, so the independent check uses the visible south-front classroom corner instead. Independent excluded check errors: 0.82 m, 3.44 m. Visible crown centers are fitted to clear trunks within the observed crown footprint (maximum seven metres); crowns may overhang roofs and roads. Crown widths in the dense belts are estimated from image pixels against their matched local roof scale; existing circular crowns approximate irregular/elliptical image crowns. Complete mapped roofs, pitches, full-width paths/roads, water and farmland remain unchanged. Planted islands take precedence over exposed paving; ground under opaque canopy is not invented. No surveyed boundary, species, construction date or exact inventory inferred; no bitmap ships."
